    "scientific_conclusion": "Even when mechanical work is precisely measured in Joules across 567 repeated sprint bouts, a cumulative work model improves MAE by only +0.53 W over a simple mean retention baseline, with a 95% CI of [-2.96, +4.29] W crossing zero. Adding recovery duration does not improve prediction (dMAE = -0.25 W [-3.87, +3.70] W). Mechanical work alone does not resolve individual residual capacity."
